│       (default: 1)                                                           │
│ --observation.history-length-dict.depth-obs INT                              │
│       (default: 3)                                                           │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─ task options ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Task execution configuration.                                                │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ --task.model-path STR|[STR,...]                                              │
│       Path to ONNX model(s). Supports local paths and wandb:// URIs.         │
│       Required field.                                                        │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│       Most policies take a single path. Composite policies take an ordered   │
│       list of                                                                │
│       the models they compose — e.g. depth distillation takes exactly        │
│       ``[depth_backbone.onnx, student.onnx]``. This differs from the         │
│       multi-policy                                                           │
│       case, where a list means several independently switchable policies.    │
│       (default: '')                                                          │
│ --task.policy-type STR                                                       │
│       Explicit policy class selector, resolved against the                   │
│       ``holosoma.policies.by_type`` entry-point group. Empty means infer the │
│       class                                                                  │
│       from the observation/robot heuristic. (default: depth_distillation)    │
│ --task.record-dir STR                                                        │
│       Subdirectory under ``recorded_motion/`` for saved motion clips.        │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│       Empty means ``"default_run"``. Recording is armed with the ``c`` key   │
│       while                                                                  │
│       the policy is running, not by setting this field. (default: '')        │
│ --task.record-label STR                                                      │
│       Filename label for recorded clips. Clips are written to                │
│       ``recorded_motion/<record_dir>/<record_label>_duration<X.X>s_motion.np │
│       z``. (default: clip)                                                   │
│ --task.rl-rate FLOAT                                                         │
│       Policy inference rate in Hz. (default: 50.0)                           │
│ --task.policy-action-scale FLOAT                                             │
│       Scaling factor applied to policy actions. (default: 1.0)               │
│ --task.action-scales-by-effort-limit-over-p-gain,                            │
│ --task.no-action-scales-by-effort-limit-over-p-gain                          │
│       Use per-joint scaling: ``policy_action_scale * effort_limit /          │
│       p_gain``. (default: False)                                             │
│ --task.use-phase, --task.no-use-phase                                        │
│       Whether to use gait phase observations. (default: False)               │
│ --task.gait-period FLOAT                                                     │
│       Gait cycle period in seconds. (default: 1.0)                           │
│ --task.skip-stiff-prompt, --task.no-skip-stiff-prompt                        │
│       WBT: skip the blocking stdin prompt before entering stiff hold and     │
│       enter                                                                  │
│       immediately. Default False keeps the interactive 'Press Enter to       │
│       continue'                                                              │
│       safety pause; non-interactive launches (e.g. the ROS2 service node)    │
│       set True. (default: False)                                             │
│ --task.domain-id INT                                                         │
│       DDS domain ID for communication. (default: 0)                          │
│ --task.interface STR                                                         │
│       Network interface name. Use ``"auto"`` to auto-detect, or specify      │
│       explicitly (e.g. ``"eth0"``). (default: lo)                            │
│ --task.velocity-input {keyboard,interface,joystick,ros2,injected}            │
│       Source for velocity commands. (default: keyboard)                      │
│ --task.state-input {keyboard,interface,joystick,ros2,injected}               │
│       Source for non-velocity inputs (start/stop, walk/stand, tuning).       │
│       (default: keyboard)                                                    │
│ --task.use-keyboard, --task.no-use-keyboard                                  │
│       Shortcut: set both velocity_input and state_input to "keyboard".       │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│       Cannot be combined with explicit input settings. (default: False)      │
│ --task.use-joystick, --task.no-use-joystick                                  │
│       Shortcut: set both velocity_input and state_input to "interface".      │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│       Reads from the SDK's wireless controller (the dongle/controller        │
│       shipped                                                                │
│       with Unitree G1, Booster T1, etc.). For host-side USB gamepads         │
│       (Xbox/Logitech via /dev/input/event*), use ``use_usb_joystick``        │
│       instead.                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│       Cannot be combined with explicit input settings. (default: False)      │
│ --task.use-usb-joystick, --task.no-use-usb-joystick                          │
│       Shortcut: set both velocity_input and state_input to "joystick".       │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│       Reads a USB gamepad on the host via evdev (``/dev/input/event*``).     │
│       Linux-only. Cannot be combined with explicit input settings. (default: │
│       False)                                                                 │
│ --task.joystick-type STR                                                     │
│       Joystick type. (default: xbox)                                         │
│ --task.joystick-device INT                                                   │
│       Joystick device index. (default: 0)                                    │
│ --task.ros-cmd-vel-topic STR                                                 │
│       ROS2 topic name for velocity commands (used when velocity_input is     │
│       "ros2"). (default: cmd_vel)                                            │
│ --task.ros-state-input-topic STR                                             │
│       ROS2 topic name for discrete commands (used when state_input is        │
│       "ros2"). (default: holosoma/state_input)                               │
│ --task.ros-vel-timeout FLOAT                                                 │
│       Seconds without a velocity message before zeroing commands. Set to 0   │
│       to disable. (default: 1.0)                                             │
│ --task.auto-walk-on-vel-cmd, --task.no-auto-walk-on-vel-cmd                  │
│       Automatically enter walking mode when a non-zero velocity command is   │
│       received. (default: False)                                             │
│ --task.use-sim-time, --task.no-use-sim-time                                  │
│       Use synchronized simulation time for WBT policies. (default: False)    │
│ --task.desired-base-height FLOAT                                             │
│       Target base height in meters. (default: 0.75)                          │
│ --task.residual-upper-body-action, --task.no-residual-upper-body-action      │
│       Whether to use residual control for upper body. (default: False)       │
│ --task.print-observations, --task.no-print-observations                      │
│       Print observation vectors for debugging. (default: False)              │
│ --task.motion-start-timestep INT                                             │
│       Starting timestep for motion clip playback. (default: 0)               │
│ --task.motion-end-timestep {None}|INT                                        │
│       Ending timestep for motion clip playback. If None, plays until the     │
│       end. (default: None)                                                   │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─ task.depth-shm options ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Shared-memory depth transport (used when the policy consumes depth images    │
│ and no ROS2 depth consumer is configured).                                   │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ --task.depth-shm.name STR                                                    │
│       Shared-memory block name, must match the producer's. (default:         │
│       depth_img_shm)                                                         │
│ --task.depth-shm.required, --task.depth-shm.no-required                      │
│       Fail policy startup if the block is absent.                            │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│       ``False`` substitutes zero frames and logs a warning, which lets the   │
│       policy                                                                 │
│       run without a depth producer (useful for smoke-testing the control     │
│       loop). (default: True)                                                 │
│ --task.depth-shm.heartbeat, --task.depth-shm.no-heartbeat                    │
│       Follow the producer's liveness heartbeat and stop the policy if depth  │
│       goes stale.                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│       Producers that do not publish one keep working; the policy logs one    │
│       warning                                                                │
│       and leaves liveness unchecked. (default: True)                         │
│ --task.depth-shm.heartbeat-endpoint STR                                      │
│       zmq endpoint of the heartbeat. Empty uses                              │
│       ``ipc:///tmp/<name>.heartbeat``. (default: '')                         │
│ --task.depth-shm.stale-warn-s FLOAT                                          │
│       Warn once the depth frame has not advanced for this many seconds.      │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│       Must exceed the producer's frame period: the D435i (and the sim        │
│       plugin's default                                                       │
│       ``render_hz``) publishes at 10 Hz, so a healthy stream already goes    │
│       0.1 s between                                                          │
│       frames. 0.25 s is about 2.5 missed frames. (default: 0.25)             │
│ --task.depth-shm.stale-stop-s FLOAT                                          │
│       Enter stiff hold once the depth frame has not advanced for this many   │
│       seconds                                                                │
│       (5 missed frames at 10 Hz), or as soon as the producer reports FAILED. │
│       The                                                                    │
│       operator resumes with ``]``. (default: 0.5)                            │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─ task.depth options ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Depth-image consumer config (empty ``topics`` disables it).                  │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ --task.depth.topics (STR,...)                                                │
│       Raw depth topic(s) (``sensor_msgs/Image``, encoding ``32FC1``, metric  │
│       meters). Empty disables the sensor. One per camera, in stack order     │
│       (front                                                                 │
│       first, back second). Multi-camera frames are time-synchronized; the    │
│       policy                                                                 │
│       reads a preprocessed ``(N, 1, resized_height, resized_width)`` stack   │
│       via                                                                    │
│       ``self._injected_sensors["depth"].get_latest()``. (default: '()')      │
│ --task.depth.resized-height INT                                              │
│       Target height (bicubic resize) before clip+normalize. (default: 27)    │
│ --task.depth.resized-width INT                                               │
│       Target width (bicubic resize) before clip+normalize. (default: 48)     │
│ --task.depth.near-clip FLOAT                                                 │
│       Near clip (m); depth is normalized to [-0.5, 0.5] over [near, far].    │
│       (default: 0.1)                                                         │
│ --task.depth.far-clip FLOAT                                                  │
│       Far clip (m); depth is normalized to [-0.5, 0.5] over [near, far].     │
│       (default: 2.0)                                                         │
│ --task.depth.frame-delay-ms FLOAT                                            │
│       Modeled depth latency to re-introduce, in absolute milliseconds.       │
│                                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│       The ROS2 depth transport is effectively instantaneous (sub-1ms), but   │
│       the                                                                    │
│       policy was trained with the on-robot image_server's inherent           │
│       capture/serve                                                          │
│       latency baked in. ``get_latest()`` holds back frames so it returns the │
│       freshest frame at least this old, reproducing that delay independent   │
│       of                                                                     │
│       publish rate (a fixed ms value is robust across fps, unlike a frame    │
│       count).                                                                │
│       ``0.0`` (default) keeps freshest-frame behavior. Pin this per-policy   │
│       from a                                                                 │
│       preset to match the delay the model was trained with (e.g. ``200.0``). │
│       (default: 0.0)                                                         │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─ task.debug options ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Debug overrides for quick testing.                                           │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ --task.debug.force-upright-imu, --task.debug.no-force-upright-imu            │
│       Override projected_gravity with [0, 0, -1] (perfectly upright).        │
│       (default: False)                                                       │
│ --task.debug.force-zero-angular-velocity,                                    │
│ --task.debug.no-force-zero-angular-velocity                                  │
│       Override base_ang_vel with [0, 0, 0]. (default: False)                 │
│ --task.debug.force-zero-action, --task.debug.no-force-zero-action            │
│       Zero out the scaled policy action (robot holds default pose).          │
│       (default: False)                                                       │
│ --task.debug.record-rosbag, --task.debug.no-record-rosbag                    │
│       Record a per-session rosbag for the lifetime of this run_policy        │
│       process.                                                               │
│       Spawns ``ros2 bag record --all`` in the background when the policy     │
│       starts and                                                             │
│       stops it on exit (Ctrl-C, normal completion, or error), then prints    │
│       the bag's                                                              │
│       absolute path. Each run gets its own short, self-contained bag — no    │
│       hunting                                                                │
│       for a timestamp inside a long fleet-telemetry recording. (default:     │
│       False)                                                                 │
│ --task.debug.rosbag-dir STR                                                  │
│       Directory for per-session rosbags recorded via ``record_rosbag``.      │
│       (default: '~/run_policy_sessions')                                     │
│ --task.debug.rosbag-cpu INT                                                  │
│       CPU core to pin ``ros2 bag record`` to (via ``taskset``) so it doesn't │
│       inherit the policy's affinity and add control-loop jitter. Default 0   │
│       exists                                                                 │
│       everywhere and is never an isolated RT core. Negative disables         │
│       pinning. (default: 0)                                                  │
